---
import ContentLayout from "astro-theme-university/layouts/ContentLayout.astro";
import SessionsGrid from "../../components/SessionsGrid.astro";
import { sessionLabels, siteConfig } from "../../site-config";
---

<ContentLayout
  title={sessionLabels.plural}
  description="What happens in the room each week, what to bring, and how it relates to the target you are carrying."
  {...siteConfig}
>
  <p>
    Each week you apply that week's technique to one program. Where your
    assignment target suits the technique, use it — the work counts twice, and
    several weeks are built so that it will. Where it does not suit, take one
    of the suggestions offered; understanding a technique your own target does
    not need is most of what the course is for.
  </p>
  <p>
    No target fits all twelve weeks. Week 3 wants something written in
    JavaScript; week 9 wants something you can obtain as a compiled binary;
    week 11 wants something that draws. Suggestions are given every week so
    that nobody spends the hour deciding what to work on.
  </p>
  <p>
    Because the room is working on different programs, the comparison across
    the room is the part you cannot get alone — the same technique against a
    dozen targets, succeeding and failing for reasons you would never have
    hit yourself. Bring a laptop, and something you are prepared to be wrong
    about.
  </p>
  <SessionsGrid />
</ContentLayout>
